    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d63">

                <pb facs="0484" n="470" xml:id="pg470"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rush, Acting
                        Secretary of State, to Mr. McCulloch,
                        collector.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                        State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1817-03-21"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">March</hi> 21, 1817</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By a letter of this date the attorney of
                    the United States has been requested to furnish every *information in his power
                    relative to alleged outfits of several vessels at Baltimore. The subject being
                    deemed of importance at this Department, I have to request that you will be so
                    obliging as to afford that officer all the aid in your power toward the objects
                    which the letter to him embraces. He will show it to you, and I have to add how
                    desirable it is that the information which it calls for should be obtained in a
                    manner the most ample and exact that is practicable. <seg type="margin"
                        >[60]</seg></p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RICHARD RUSH,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of
                            State.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Collector</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of Baltimore.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
